---
import MainLayout from "../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
---

<MainLayout>

  <section class="hero">

    <img
      src="/SVG-DBR-LOGO.png"
      alt="Dual Brain Robotics Logo"
      class="hero-logo"
    />

    <h1>Dual Brain Robotics</h1>

    <h2>A New Architecture for Conscious Machines</h2>

    <p>
      Developed by Dr. Alexander Durig, Dual Brain Robotics proposes
      a bilateral cognitive architecture inspired by the cooperative
      processing systems of the human brain.
    </p>

    <p>
      Provisional Patent Pending
    </p>

    <p class="patent-status">
      U.S. Utility-Provisional Patent Application<br />
      Dual Brain Robotics Architecture<br />
      Application No. 64/181,346
    </p>

    <a href="/architecture" class="button">
      Explore the Architecture
    </a>

  </section>

  <section class="section">

    <h2>The Robotics Challenge</h2>

    <p>
      Modern robots can perform highly precise tasks in structured
      environments, yet many continue to struggle with smooth,
      adaptive, and highly coordinated movement.
    </p>

    <p>
      Dual Brain Robotics explores whether a bilateral cognitive
      architecture can support more natural robotic movement,
      dexterity, coordination, and environmental adaptation.
    </p>

  </section>

  <section class="section">

    <h2>The Proposed Solution</h2>

    <p>
      Dual Brain Robotics introduces a framework in which autonomous
      systems process information through interacting cognitive
      channels rather than a single decision stream.
    </p>

  </section>

  <section class="section">

    <h2>Research Foundation</h2>

    <p>
      The architecture emerges from decades of work in social
      psychology, perception theory, autism research, and the
      study of consciousness.
    </p>
<p>This site presents...</p>

<p>An inventor.</p>

<p>A theory.</p>

<p>A patent filing.</p>

<p>A research foundation.</p>

<p>A robotics application.</p>

<p>And how those pieces reinforce one another.</p>
<p>


<p>"What is Dual Brain Robotics?"</p>
<p>


<p>"Why would anyone build this?"</p>


<p>
<p>The answer lies in exploring the possibility of:
<ul>
<li>smoother robotic movement</li>
<li>improved dexterity</li>
<li>bilateral error correction</li>
<li>micro-coordination</li>
<li>adaptive behavior</li>
<li>more natural interaction with real-world environments</li>
</ul>
</p>
<p>Those are tangible engineering goals.
<p>
<p>The only question left now is,</p>
<p>"Is this a theory of consciousness applied to robotics?"</p>
<p>
<p>or</p>
<p>
<p>"Is this a robotics architecture inspired by a theory of consciousness?"</p>
  </section>

</MainLayout>
